hadiths[104]{hadithnumber,text}:
"7844","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Yahya bin Ayyub told me Al-Misri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Zuhar, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Imran, on the authority of Amr bin Murrah Al-Jamali, on the authority of Muadh bin Jabal, may God be pleased with him He said to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when he sent him to Yemen: O Messenger of God, advise me. He said: “Finish your religion, and your work will suffice for you.” “This is a small hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”[Comment - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7844 - Incorrect"
"7845","Bakr bin Muhammad Al-Sayrifi told us, Bamru, Abdul-Samad bin Al-Fadl Al-Balkhi told us, Makki bin Ibrahim told us, Abdullah bin Saeed told us Ibn Abi Hind, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Two blessings that are unjustified.” Many people: health and free time “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7845 - This in Al-Bukhari"
"7846","Al-Hasan bin Halim Al-Marwazi informed me, Abu Al-Mawjih informed, Abdan informed, Abdullah bin Abi Hind informed, about... His father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to a man while he was advising him: “Take advantage of five before Five: your youth before your old age, your health before your illness, your wealth before your poverty, your free time before your work, and your life before Your death “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7846 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7847","Muhammad ibn Salih ibn Hani told me, Al-Sari ibn Khuzaymah told me, Saeed ibn Sulaiman Al-Wasiti Sa’dawiya told me, Zakaria ibn Manzur told me. Ibn Tha'labah Ibn Abi Malik, Abu Hazim narrated to us, on the authority of Sahl Ibn Sa'd, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by a Then he saw a sheep with one leg strayed and said: “Do you think this sheep is easy for its owner?” They said: Yes. He said: “By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, this world is easier for God than this for its owner, even if the world were equal to God.” “The wing of a mosquito does not give an unbeliever a drink of water from it.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7847 - Zakaria bin Manzur is weak"
"7848","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told me, Bishr bin Musa told us, Khalid bin Khadash bin Ajlan Al-Muhallabi told us, Abd told us Allah bin Wahb, on the authority of Hisham bin Saad, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yassar, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him He said: I entered upon the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, while he was feverish, so I put my hand on top of the velvet and felt the heat of his fever and said: How intense your fever is, O Messenger of God. He said: “We are like that, community of prophets. The pain will be doubled for us so that the reward will be doubled for us.” He said: So I said: O Messenger of God, that is. People are more afflicted? He said: “The Prophets.” I said: Then who? He said: “Then are the righteous. If a man is afflicted with poverty until he finds nothing but a cloak, he covers it and wears it, and if one of them He will be plagued with lice until the lice kills him, and that is more beloved to them than giving to you.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and it was not “He brings him out.”[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7848 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"7849","Abu Al-Nadr Al-Faqih and Ibrahim bin Ismail Al-Qari told us, saying: Uthman bin Saeed Al-Darimi told us, Yahya bin Saleh told us. Al-Wahazi, Abu Ismail Al-Sakouni told us, he said: I heard Malik bin Adi saying: I heard Al-Nu’man bin Bashir, may God be pleased with them both, saying, and he On the pulpit: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Indeed, nothing remains of the world except the likes of flies passing through its atmosphere. By God “God bless your brothers among the people of the graves, for your deeds will be presented to them.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7849 - It contains two unknowns"
"7850","Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Abu Bakr bin Abi Al-Dunya told us, Suwayd bin Saeed told me, Baqiya bin Al-Walid told me, on the authority of Buhair bin Saad, on the authority of Khaled bin Maadan, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah bin Al-Jarrah, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The heart of the son of Adam is like a bird, turning over seven times a day.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7850 - There is an interruption"
"7851","Abdullah bin Al-Hussein Al-Qadi told me about Marw, Al-Harith bin Abi Usama told us, Abu Al-Nadr Hashim bin Al-Qasim told us, Abu Aqeel told us Al-Thaqafi, on the authority of Yazid bin Sinan, on the authority of Bukair bin Fayrouz, saying: He heard Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, say: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: And he said: “Whoever is afraid will go in, and whoever goes in will have reached the final destination. Indeed, God’s goodness is precious. Indeed, God’s goodness is precious.” This is an authentic hadith. The chain of transmission and they did not narrate it.”[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7851 - True"
"7852","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ali bin Al-Hasan Al-Hilali told us, Abdullah bin Al-Walid Al-Adni told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel, on the authority of Tufail bin Ubayy bin Ka’b, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever fears He entered and whoever entered has reached the final destination. Indeed, God’s commodity is precious. Verily, God’s commodity is Paradise, the trembling one has come, followed by the equivalent one, it has come. “Death and all that is in it”[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7852 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7853","Abu Al-Hasan Muhammad bin Ali bin Bukayr, Al-Adl, told us, Al-Fadl bin Muhammad bin Al-Musayyab Al-Sha’arani told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Mundhir told us, Abdul Aziz bin Muhammad told us, Amr bin Abi Amr told us, on the authority of Al-Muttalib bin Abdullah bin Hantab, on the authority of Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari, may God be pleased with him. On his authority, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever loves his world will be harmed by his hereafter, and whoever loves his hereafter will be harmed by his worldly life, so choose what “It endures as it perishes.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7853 - There is a break"
"7854","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, Abu Al-Muthanna told us, Musaddad told us, Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Saad bin Ishaq bin Ka’b. Ibn Ujrah, on the authority of Zainab bint Kaab, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him. A man said: O Messenger of God, have you seen these diseases that It afflicts us, what do we do with it? He said: “Atonements.” Ubayy bin Ka’b said: O Messenger of God, even if it is small? He said: “A thorn, and what is above it?” He said: “Then my father prayed for himself that the illness would not leave him until he died after not distracting him from Hajj, Umrah, or jihad in the path of God. “There is no prescribed prayer in congregation.” He said: “No man touched his skin after that except that he felt its heat until he died.” This is an authentic hadith subject to the conditions. The two sheikhs did not narrate it.”[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7854 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7855","Al-Hasan bin Halim Al-Marwazi informed me, Abu Al-Mujih informed me, Abdan informed me, Abdullah informed me, Rishdin informed me, about... Amr bin Al-Harith, Yazid bin Abi Habib told me that Abu Al-Khair told him that he heard Uqba bin Amir Al-Juhani, may God be pleased with him. On the authority of him, he narrates on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “There is not a day’s work that is not completed. When a believer falls ill, the angels say: Oh. Our Lord, Your servant is so-and-so whom You have imprisoned. Then the Almighty Lord says: Conclude for him according to his deeds, until he recovers or dies. This is an authentic hadith. The chain of transmission and they did not narrate it.”[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7855 - Rushdin Wah"
"7856","Ahmad bin Abdullah Al-Muzani told us, Abdullah bin Najiya told us, Ubayd Allah bin Omar Al-Qawariri told us, Abd al-Samad bin Abd al-Warith, Abd al-Wahid ibn Zayd told us, Aslam al-Kufi told me, on the authority of Murrat al-Tayyib, on the authority of Zayd ibn Arqam, he said: We were with Abu Bakr. Al-Siddiq, may God be pleased with him, called for a drink and it was brought water and honey. When he brought it to his mouth, he cried and cried until his companions cried, but they remained silent, but he did not remain silent. Then he came back and cried until they thought they would not be able to ask him. He said: Then he wiped his eyes and they said: O successor of the Messenger of God, may God bless him. What made you cry? He said: I was with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I saw him defending something from himself, but I did not see anyone with him, so I said: O Messenger of God, what are you defending? About yourself? He said: “This world appeared to me, so I said to it, ‘Away with me,’ then she came back and said, ‘If I escape from me, no one will escape from me after you.’” This A hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7856 - Abd Al-Samad, left by Al-Bukhari and others"
"7857","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Shaybani told us, Ali bin Al-Hasan Al-Hilali told us, Muhammad bin Jahdam told us, Ismail bin Jafar, on the authority of Amara bin Ghaziyah, on the authority of Asim bin Omar bin Qatada, on the authority of Mahmoud bin Labid, on the authority of Qatada bin Al-Numan, may God be pleased with him He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If God loves a servant, he protects him in this world just as one of you protects his sick person with water.” This is an authentic hadith. According to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7857 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7858","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Muhammad bin Ghalib told us, Musa bin Ismail told us, Thabit bin Yazid told us, Hilal bin Khabbab told us, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, said: Omar Ibn Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, entered upon the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, while he was on the Mat affected his side and he said: O Messenger of God, if you had a better bed than this, he said: “What do I have to do with this world? What does this world have to do with me?” By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, my likeness and the likeness of this world are nothing but like a rider who rode on a summer day and stayed in the shade under a tree for an hour of the day, then departed. “And he left it.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari, but they did not narrate it. “And this is witnessed by the hadith of Abdullah bin Masoud.”[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7858 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7859","Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdul-Wahhab bin Habib told us, Ja’far bin Aoun told us, Al-Masoudi informed us, on the authority of Amr bin Once, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah, may God be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I have nothing to do with this world. I am only like myself.” The example of this world is that of a rider who sat under a tree on a summer day and left it."
"7860","Abu Ali Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Hafiz and Abu Al-Hasan Ali bin Bandar Al-Zahid told us, saying: Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Al-Hasan informed us Al-Asqalani, Ibrahim bin Amr Al-Saskiki told us, Abi told us, Abdul Aziz bin Abi Rawad told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar, may God be pleased with him. On the authority of them, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever seeks what is with God, the sky will be his shade and the earth his bed. He will not care about anything.” The matter of the world, he does not plant crops while eating bread, and he does not plant trees and eat fruits out of trust in God Almighty and seeking To please Him, so God has guaranteed the seven heavens and the seven earths His provision. They labor over it and bring it lawful, and He completes His provision without anything else. An account with God Almighty until certainty comes to him.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration for the Syrians, but they did not narrate it.[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7860 - Rather, it is objectionable or fabricated"
"7861","Abdullah bin Ja`far al-Quta’i told us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Abu al-Mughirah told us, Safwan told us Ibn Amr, on the authority of Shurayh Ibn Ubaid, that Abu Malik Al-Ash’ari, when death approached him, said: O community of Ash’aris, let the witness be informed. Among you who is absent is that I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “The bitterness of this world is the bitterness of the hereafter.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7861 - True"
"7862","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan told us, Zayd bin Al-Hubab told us, Sufyan Al-Thawri told us, on the authority of Al-Mughirah Al-Khorasani, on the authority of Al-Rabi’ ibn Anas, on the authority of Abu Al-Aliyah, on the authority of Ubayy ibn Ka’b, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Give glad tidings to this nation of prosperity, exaltation, victory, and empowerment on earth, and whoever among them does the work of the Hereafter for this world will not have it in it.” The Hereafter is a share.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7862 - True"
"7863","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Balawayh told me, Muhammad bin Bishr bin Matar told me, Muhammad bin Ja’far al-Warkani told me, Adi bin Al-Fadl, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abdullah Al-Masoudi, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, may God be pleased with him On his authority, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited: {So whomever God wishes to guide, He will open his chest to Islam} [Al-An’am: 125] So the Messenger of God said May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “When light enters the chest, it is revealed.” It was said: O Messenger of God, does this have any knowledge that can be known? He said: “Yes, avoiding the abode of deception, turning to the abode of eternity, and preparing for death before it descends.”[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7863 - Adi bin Al-Fadl has fallen"
"7864","Ibrahim bin Asmah bin Ibrahim, Al-Adl told me, my father told us, Yahya bin Yahya told us, Abu Muawiyah told me, on the authority of Al-Awwam bin Juwayriyah, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Four things are not afflicted except with astonishment: silence.” It is the beginning of worship, humility, remembrance of God Almighty, and the lack of something.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it. Fahd bin Awf, Omar bin Al-Fadl narrated to us, on the authority of Raqaba bin Masqala, on the authority of Ali bin Al-Aqmar, on the authority of Abu Juhayfah, he said: I ate meat A lot and a lot of porridge. Then I came and sat next to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I burped. He said: “Short your belches, for most people are full.” In this world, the hungriest are the ones in the hereafter.” True."
"7865","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Amrwayh Al-Bazzaz told us, in Baghdad, Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, Al-Hasan bin Musa told us Al-Ashayb, Uqba bin Abdullah Al-Asam told us, Abdullah bin Buraidah told us, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said May God bless him and grant him peace: “When a man says to a hypocrite, ‘O my master, he has angered his Lord, Blessed and Most High.’ This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7865 - Uqba bin Al-Asam is weak"
"7866","Ahmad ibn Abi Uthman al-Zahid told me, Ibrahim ibn Abi Talib told me, Abd al-Warith ibn Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith told me, My father, Harith bin Al-Sa’ib narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Hamran bin Aban, on the authority of Uthman bin Affan, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “The son of Adam has no right to anything except these qualities: a house to cover him, a garment to cover his private parts, and a sack of bread and water.” “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7866 - True"
"7867","Ja`far bin Muhammad al-Khalidi told us, Abu al-Abbas told us, on the authority of Masruq, Shurayh bin Yunus told us, Sa`id bin Muhammad al-Warraq told us, Salih bin Hassan, on the authority of Urwa ibn al-Zubayr, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: “O Aisha, if... You want to join me, so let this world be enough for you like a rider’s provisions. Do not make a garment until you patch it, and beware of sitting with the rich.” This is a hadith. The chain of narration is authentic, but they did not narrate it.”"
"7868","Hamza bin Al-Abbas Al-Aqbi told us, Abu Qalaba told us, Ishaq bin Nasih told us, Shayban told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Raba’i bin Harash, on the authority of Tariq bin Abdullah Al-Muharbi, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “O Tariq, prepare for death.” “Before the descent of death” is true.[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7868 - True"
"7869","Abdullah bin Al-Shakhir told us, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Leave income to the rich, for it is possible that you do not despise The blessings of God Almighty. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7869 - True"
"7870","Ahmad bin Kamil Al-Qadi told us, Ja’far bin Abi Othman Al-Tayalisi told us, Yahya bin Ayyub told us, Abdul-Jabbar bin Wahb told us, Saad bin Tariq reported on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The blessings of the worldly abode are for those who provide From it to his hereafter until his Lord, the Mighty and Majestic, is satisfied. And wretched is the abode for he who turns him away from his hereafter and falls short of his Lord’s satisfaction, and when The servant said, “God is disgraceful to the world.” The world said, “God is disgraceful to those who disobey their Lord.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7870 - Rather, it is objectionable"
"7871","Abu Ja`far Ahmad ibn Ubaid al-Hafiz told us, in Hamadan, Ibrahim ibn al-Hussein told us, Abu al-Yaman told us, Ufair ibn Ma`dan told us, on the authority of Sulaym bin Amir, on the authority of Abu Umamah, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When a servant becomes ill, God inspires His angels: O my angels, I have bound My servant with one of My fetters. If I seize him, I will forgive him, and if I pardon him, then he will sit and not commit any sin. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7871 - Afeer bin Ma’dan is weak"
"7872","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, may God be pleased with him, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever dies doing something, God will resurrect him for it.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration. The condition of a Muslim and they did not narrate it.”[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7872 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"7873","Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ja`far al-Aadmi al-Qari, in Baghdad, narrated to us, Abu Ja`far Ahmad ibn Ubaid ibn Nasih narrated to us, Khalid ibn Nasih narrated to us. Amr Al-Qurashi, Sufyan Al-Thawri narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Sahl bin Saad, may God be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, advised a man He said: “Avoid the world and God Almighty will love you, and abstain from what is in the hands of people and the people will love you.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7873 - Khalid bin Amr Al-Qurashi is lost"
"7874","Ibrahim bin Asmah bin Ibrahim, Al-Adl told me, my father told us, Yahya bin Yahya told us, Ibrahim bin Saad told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman bin Ma’iz Al-Amiri, on the authority of Sufyan bin Abdullah Al-Thaqafi, may God be pleased with him, who said: I said: O Messenger God spoke to me about something that I should adhere to. He said: “Say, ‘My Lord is God, then be upright.’” He said: I said: O Messenger of God, how much do I fear for myself? He said: So he took his breath and then said: “This” is “a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.”[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7874 - True"
"7875","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Ghalib told us, Ishaq bin Abdul-Wahid al-Qurashi told us, Hushaym told us, on the authority of Abdul Al-Rahman bin Ishaq, on the authority of Muharib bin Dathar, on the authority of Silah bin Zufar, on the authority of Hudhayfah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “A look is one of Satan’s poisoned arrows. Whoever abandons it out of fear of God, the Almighty and Majestic, will reward him with faith that will find its sweetness in his heart.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”"
"7876","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bakr bin Sahl Al-Damiati told us, Shuaib bin Yahya told us, Ibn Lahi’ah told us, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Yazid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, may God be pleased with them both, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “If you have four, it will not matter what you missed. “This world: keeping trustworthiness, truthfulness in speech, good character, and chaste food.”[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7876 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7877","Abu Hafs bin Omar bin Muhammad bin Ahmed Al-Jumahi told us, in Mecca in the house of Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq, Ali bin Abdul Aziz told us, Ahmad bin Issa Al-Masry told us, on the authority of Amr bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Darraj, on the authority of Abu Al-Haytham, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If a man did work in a rock that has no door or opening, his work would go out to the people in some form.” “This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7877 - True"
"7878","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ""Indeed, Allah tries each one of you with balāʾ (tribulations) while He is well aware of him. ˹He tries him˺ just like one of you ˹purifies˺ his gold with fire. 7879"""
"7879","Muhammad bin Abdullah al-Zahid informed us, Abu Bakr bin Abi al-Dunya al-Qurashi narrated to us, Ishaq bin Kab narrated to us, Abbad bin al-Awwam narrated to us, from Muhammad bin Amr, from Abi Salamah, from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Affliction does not cease with the believer in his body and wealth until he meets Allah, Exalted, with no sin upon him. This hadith is sahih according to the condition of Muslim, but they did not narrate it. [Commentary - from al-Dhahabi's summary] 7879 - According to the condition of Muslim."
"7880","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh narrated to us, Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Umarah bin Umayr, from Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid, who said: Abdullah said: You pray more and fast more than the Companions of Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, yet they were better than you. They said: How? He said: They were more detached from this world than you and more desirous of the Hereafter than you. This hadith is sahih according to the condition of the two Shaykhs, but they did not narrate it. [Commentary - from al-Dhahabi's summary] 7880 - According to the condition of al-Bukhari and Muslim."
"7881","Amr bin al-As, may Allah be pleased with him, delivered a sermon on the pulpit, saying: By Allah, I have never seen a people more desirous of what the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was most detached from. You love this world greatly, while the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, paid it no heed. By Allah, three consecutive days never passed upon the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in which his needs did not exceed his means. This hadith is sahih according to the condition of al-Bukhari, but the two Shaykhs did not narrate it."
"7882","Abdullah bin Amr, may Allah be pleased with them, narrates that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The world is a prison for the believer, and a famine; when he leaves the world, he leaves prison and famine."
"7883","Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: In the end of time there will be ignorant worshippers and corrupt reciters."
"7884","Abu al-Darda, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah loves the troubled heart. This hadith is sahih al-isnad but Imam Bukhari and Imam Muslim did not narrate it."
"7885","Asma bint Umays al-Khathamiyyah, may Allah be pleased with her, narrates that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: How evil is the servant who considers himself great and is arrogant, forgetting the Great and Exalted (Allah). How evil is the servant who forgets and indulges in play, forgetting the beginning and the end. How evil is the servant who rebels and disobeys, forgetting the grave and the trial. How evil is the servant who mixes the world with religion. How evil is the servant who creates doubts in religion. How evil is the servant whom awe keeps away from the truth. How evil is the servant who follows greed. How evil is the servant whose desires keep him astray. No narrator in its chain is impugned in any way, so this hadith is sahih, but Imam Bukhari and Imam Muslim did not narrate it."
"7886","Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: You will be selected as dates are selected from a basket of dates; the good people will be taken up and the wicked will remain. So die if you can. This hadith is sahih al-isnad but Imam Bukhari and Imam Muslim did not narrate it; in its chain is Abu Jamil al-Tai."
"7887","Abu Said al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates from Bilal, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O Bilal, meet Allah in poverty, not in wealth. Bilal said: I asked: O Messenger of Allah, how will that be? He said: When you receive provision, do not store it, and when you are asked, do not refuse. I said: O Messenger of Allah, what will be its outcome? He said: If you do so, it is well; otherwise you will enter the Fire. This hadith is sahih al-isnad but Imam Bukhari and Imam Muslim did not narrate it."
"7888","Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered Mecca at the conquest of Mecca so bowed in humility that his chin nearly touched his saddle. This hadith is sahih according to the condition of Imam Muslim, but the two Shaykhs did not narrate it."
"7889","Hudhayfah, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever wakes in the morning with his greatest hope being this world has no connection with Allah; whoever does not fear Allah has no connection with Allah; and whoever does not care for the generality of Muslims is not among them (the Muslims)."
"7890","Jadah al-Jushami, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, pointing with his hand toward the belly of a stout man, saying: What is in this, had it been in another's belly, would have been better for you. This hadith is sahih al-isnad but Imam Bukhari and Imam Muslim did not narrate it."
"7891","Abu Sufyan narrates from his teachers that Sad, may Allah be pleased with him, visited Salman to inquire after his health. Salman, may Allah be pleased with him, wept. Sad, may Allah be pleased with him, said: O Abu Abdullah, why do you weep, while the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, left this world pleased with you; you will meet him at his Pond, and you will meet your companions? Salman, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I do not weep from fear of death nor from greed for the world; rather I weep because I could not fulfil the covenant I made with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. In his life and for after him, he took from us the pledge that our share of the world should be only like a traveller's provision; yet around me you see these cushions, a tub for washing clothes, a large cup for drinking water, and a water jug. Sad, may Allah be pleased with him, said: O Abu Abdullah, give us a counsel to follow after you. Salman said: O Sad, when you intend something, remember God in your intention; when you distribute, remember God over your hand; and when you judge, remember God in your judgment. This hadith is sahih al-isnad but Imam Bukhari and Imam Muslim did not narrate it."
"7892","Abdullah bin Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever consumes usury, his end is poverty (he ultimately becomes destitute). This hadith is sahih al-isnad but Imam Bukhari and Imam Muslim did not narrate it."
"7893","Abu Dharr, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever falsely accuses a Muslim, Allah will cast him into Hell on the Day of Resurrection in recompense. This hadith is sahih al-isnad but Imam Bukhari and Imam Muslim did not narrate it."
"7894","Umar bin al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: If you trust in Allah completely, Allah will provide for you as He provides for the birds, which go out hungry in the morning and return satiated in the evening. This hadith is sahih al-isnad but Imam Bukhari and Imam Muslim did not narrate it."
"7895","Ubayy bin Kab, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Give my community glad tidings of rain, the ascendancy of religion, and rule in the land, so long as they do not seek the world in exchange for deeds of the Hereafter. Whoever seeks the world in exchange for a deed of the Hereafter will have no share in the Hereafter. This hadith is sahih al-isnad but Imam Bukhari and Imam Muslim did not narrate it."
"7896","Kab bin Iyad, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Every community has a trial, and the trial of my community is wealth. This hadith is sahih al-isnad but Imam Bukhari and Imam Muslim did not narrate it."
"7897","Abu Musa al-Ashari, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever loves the world ruins his Hereafter; so prefer what remains over what perishes. This hadith is sahih."
"7898","Mistwar, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates: We were with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him; the world and the Hereafter were mentioned in his presence. Some said: The world is a means to attain the Hereafter; action is in it, prayer and zakat are in it. Others held that in the Hereafter is Paradise, and many things were said. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The world compared to the Hereafter is like one who dips his finger in the sea and takes it out: what sticks to it is the world, and what is in the sea is the Hereafter. This hadith is sahih al-isnad but Imam Bukhari and Imam Muslim did not narrate it."
"7899","Atiyyah bin Sad, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The servant cannot be God-fearing until he leaves even things in which there is no harm, to avoid things in which there is harm. This hadith is sahih al-isnad but Imam Bukhari and Imam Muslim did not narrate it."
"7900","Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with them, narrates that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Death is the believer's gift. This hadith is sahih al-isnad but Imam Bukhari and Imam Muslim did not narrate it."
"7901","Umm al-Muminin Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her, narrates that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Hardships befall the righteous. This hadith is sahih al-isnad but Imam Bukhari and Imam Muslim did not narrate it."
"7902","Abdullah bin Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever wakes in the morning with his hope in other than Allah has no worth in Allah's sight; and whoever does not care for the Muslims is not among them (the Muslims)."
"7903","Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them, narrates that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, pointed with his index finger, saying: Sincerity is like this; raising his hands to his shoulders, he said: Supplication is like this; then spreading his hands, he said: And humility is this, spreading his hands further. This hadith is sahih al-isnad but Imam Bukhari and Imam Muslim did not narrate it."
"7904","Abdullah bin Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah has made the whole world insignificant; what remains of the world is the little of the little. What remains is like a pond whose clear water has been drunk, leaving turbid water. This hadith is sahih al-isnad but Imam Bukhari and Imam Muslim did not narrate it."
"7905","Abu al-Darda, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: If you knew what I know, you would weep much and laugh little, go out to the mountains seeking Allah's refuge, and you would not know whether you will be saved or not. This hadith is sahih al-isnad but Imam Bukhari and Imam Muslim did not narrate it with this chain."
"7906","Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: You await either wealth that breeds insolence, poverty that causes forgetfulness (of God), a ruinous illness, dotage impairing your mind, sudden death, the Dajjal - and the Dajjal is the awaited hidden evil - or the Hour; and the Hour is most severe and bitter. Imam al-Hakim says: If Mamar bin Rashid heard from al-Maqburi, this hadith is sahih according to the standard of Imam Bukhari and Imam Muslim, but the two Shaykhs did not narrate it."
"7907","Nawwas bin Siman al-Kilabi, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: The heart is between two fingers of Allah; He keeps it firm if He wills and turns it aside if He wills. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to supplicate: O Allah, Turner of hearts, keep our hearts firm upon Your religion. And the balance is in Allah's hand; until the Hour He raises some people and lowers others. This hadith is sahih according to the standard of Imam Muslim, but the two Shaykhs did not narrate it."
"7908","Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O Ali, seek good from the merciful of my community who live in distant lands; do not ask good of the hard-hearted, for Allah's curse descends upon the hard-hearted. O Ali, Allah created goodness and created people for it, placing love of good deeds in their hearts and directing seekers of it toward them, just as He directed water toward drought-stricken land to revive it and grant life to its inhabitants thereby. O Ali, those who do good in this world will do good in the Hereafter. This hadith is sahih al-isnad but Imam Bukhari and Imam Muslim did not narrate it."
"7909","Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Remember often death, the severer of pleasures. This hadith is sahih according to the standard of Imam Muslim, but the two Shaykhs did not narrate it."
"7910","Abdullah bin Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not take up a profession, lest you become desirous of the world. This hadith is sahih al-isnad but Imam Bukhari and Imam Muslim did not narrate it."
"7911","Abu Said, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, supplicated: O Allah, keep me alive poor, cause me to die poor, and raise me among the poor. The most unfortunate is he who is poor in this world yet seized by punishment in the Hereafter. This hadith is sahih al-isnad but Imam Bukhari and Imam Muslim did not narrate it."
"7912","Abu Umayyah al-Shabani says: I asked Abu Thalabah about the verse: O you who believe, upon you is yourselves; he who strays cannot harm you when you are guided [5:105]. Abu Thalabah said: Enjoin good and forbid evil. When you see miserliness obeyed, desires followed, the world preferred, and you face a matter you must pursue, then care for yourself and leave the people to their state; for after you are days of patience, in which patience is like holding a coal; whoever does a good deed in those days will have the reward of fifty workers. This hadith is sahih al-isnad but Imam Bukhari and Imam Muslim did not narrate it."
"7913","Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates: I came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was reciting: Rivalry has distracted you until you visited the graves. Then he said: The servant says: My wealth, my wealth, while your wealth is only what you wore and wore out, ate and consumed, or gave in charity and stored for yourself. This hadith is sahih al-isnad but Imam Bukhari and Imam Muslim did not narrate it."
"7914","Bishr bin Jahhash al-Qurashi, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, placed his blessed saliva on his palm, then placed his blessed finger upon it and said: Allah, Blessed and Exalted, says: O son of Adam, can you render Me helpless, while I created you from such a thing? When I fashioned you completely and you could walk, you began amassing wealth, refusing beggars, until death approached and you readied yourself to give charity. This is not the time for charity. This hadith is sahih al-isnad but Imam Bukhari and Imam Muslim did not narrate it."
"7915","Abdullah bin Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Show Allah the modesty He deserves. We said: O Prophet of Allah, we do show modesty to Allah. He said: Modesty is not that; rather, whoever shows Allah true modesty should guard the head and its thoughts, guard the belly and what it contains, remember death and trials. Whoever desires the Hereafter abandons the adornment of the world; whoever does so shows Allah true modesty. This hadith is sahih al-isnad but Imam Bukhari and Imam Muslim did not narrate it."
"7916","Anas bin Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: A time will come upon people when they sit in mosques in circles, yet their aim is nothing but the world; they have no concern with Allah. Do not sit in their gatherings. This hadith is sahih al-isnad but Imam Bukhari and Imam Muslim did not narrate it."
"7917","Abdullah bin Masud, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The Hour is near, while greed for the world grows among people and their distance from Allah grows. This hadith is sahih al-isnad but Imam Bukhari and Imam Muslim did not narrate it."
"7918","Sulayman bin Habib al-Muharibi narrates that Abu Umamah al-Bahili says: When the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, proclaimed prophethood, Satan's followers came to him saying: The Prophet of Allah has proclaimed prophethood and his community has come into being. Satan said: Do they love the world? His disciples said: Yes. Satan said: If they truly love the world, I do not care that they do not worship idols; they cannot escape me. I shall attend them morning and evening with three things: they will take wealth unlawfully, spend it unlawfully, and withhold it from the path of right. All evils follow these three. This hadith is sahih al-isnad but Imam Bukhari and Imam Muslim did not narrate it."
"7919","Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was asked what most admits people to Paradise. He said: God-consciousness and good character. He was also asked what most admits people to Hell. He said: The mouth and the private parts. This hadith is sahih al-isnad but Imam Bukhari and Imam Muslim did not narrate it."
"7920","Numan narrates: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was often hungry, without even enough poor-quality dates to fill his stomach. This hadith is sahih according to the standard of Imam Muslim, but the two Shaykhs did not narrate it."
"7921","Sahl bin Sad, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that Jibril, peace be upon him, came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Muhammad, live as long as you will; one day you shall die. Love whom you will; one day you shall part. Do what you will; one day you shall be recompensed. Then he said: O Muhammad, the believer's honour is in night worship, and his dignity in independence from people."
"7922","Samurah, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Lineage is wealth, and nobility is God-consciousness. This hadith is sahih al-isnad but Imam Bukhari and Imam Muslim did not narrate it."
"7923","Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When Muslims hate their scholars, raise the buildings of their markets, and marry to amass wealth, Allah will impose four things upon them: famine of the age, tyranny of the ruler, treachery of officials, and the awe of the enemy."
"7924","Jabir bin Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with them, narrates that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O people, no one shall die until he has consumed his full provision. Fear Allah, and O people, be fair in seeking; take the lawful and leave the unlawful. This hadith is sahih al-isnad but Imam Bukhari and Imam Muslim did not narrate it."
"7925","Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, always ate coarse food, wore rough clothing of wool, and wore leather sandals. Al-Hasan was asked what khashin means. He said: Thick porridge, which the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, could not swallow without a sip of water. This hadith is sahih al-isnad but Imam Bukhari and Imam Muslim did not narrate it."
"7926","Miqal bin Yasar, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Your Lord, Blessed and Exalted, says: O son of Adam, free yourself for My worship; I shall fill your heart with richness and your hands with provision. O son of Adam, do not stay away from Me, lest I fill your heart with poverty and your hands with occupation. This hadith is sahih al-isnad but Imam Bukhari and Imam Muslim did not narrate it."
"7927","Amr bin al-As, may Allah be pleased with him, delivering a sermon to the people in Egypt, said: Guidance is what your Prophet gave you; the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was detached from the world, while you love the world greatly. This hadith is sahih al-isnad but Imam Bukhari and Imam Muslim did not narrate it."
"7928","Ismail bin Muhammad bin Sad bin Abi Waqqas narrates from his father, from his grandfather, that a man came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: O Messenger of Allah, give me a brief counsel. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: Despair of what is in people's hands; beware greed, for it brings immediate poverty; pray as if it is your last prayer; and avoid what you would apologise for. This hadith is sahih al-isnad but Imam Bukhari and Imam Muslim did not narrate it."
"7929","Abu Dharr, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O Abu Dharr, what do you think: is abundance of wealth richness? I said: Yes. He said: And do you consider scarcity of wealth poverty? I said: Yes. He said: It is not so; richness is richness of the heart, and poverty is poverty of the heart. The rich is he whose heart is rich, and the poor is he whose heart is poor. Then the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, asked me about a man of Quraysh: How do you consider him? I said: Whatever he asks for, he is given; wherever he is, he is admitted. Then he asked me about a man of the Ahl al-Suffah: Do you know so-and-so? I said: No, O Messenger of Allah. The Prophet kept describing him until I recognised him. I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah, I know him. The Prophet said: How do you consider him? I said: A poor man dwelling in the mosque. The Prophet said: Were the earth filled with the likes of that Qurashi, all of them together would not equal this man. I said: O Messenger of Allah, was he not given some of what the other was given? The Prophet said: If he was given those blessings, he deserves them; if he was not given some blessings, he has been given good deeds in exchange. Imam Bukhari and Imam Muslim narrated it in abridged form from al-Amash, then Zayd bin Wahb, then Abu Dharr."
"7930","Abdan bin Yazid al-Daqqaq informed us in Hamadan, Ibrahim bin al-Husayn narrated to us, Abu Mushir narrated to us, Sadaqah bin Khalid narrated to me, Abdur Rahman bin Yazid bin Jabir narrated to me, Urwah bin Muhammad bin Atiyyah narrated to me, my father narrated to me, that his father informed him, saying: I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with some people of Banu Sad bin Bakr, and I was the youngest of the group, so they left me behind with their saddles. Then they went to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he fulfilled their needs, then said: Is anyone of you left behind? They said: Yes, a boy with us whom we left behind with our saddles. He ordered them to send for me, so they came to me and said: Answer the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. So I came to him, and when he saw me he said: Allah has enriched you well, so never ask people for anything, for the upper hand gives and the lower hand takes. And the wealth of Allah is asked for and it is also granted. He says: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, spoke to me in our own tongue. This hadith is sahih al-isnad but Imam Bukhari and Imam Muslim did not narrate it."
"7931","Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The heart of an old man remains ever young in love of two things: long life and abundance of wealth. This hadith is sahih according to the standard of Imam Bukhari and Imam Muslim, but the two Shaykhs did not narrate it."
"7932","Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There are many dishevelled, dust-covered, worn-clothed people, far from people's eyes, such that if they swear an oath upon Allah, Allah fulfils their oath. This hadith is sahih al-isnad, and I think Imam Muslim narrated it through Hafs bin Abdullah bin Anas."
"7933","Zayd bin Aslam narrates from his father that Umar bin al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, went out toward the Prophet's mosque and saw Muadh bin Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, sitting near the grave of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, weeping. Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, asked: O Muadh, why are you weeping? Muadh said: I am remembering something I heard from the occupant of this grave. Umar asked: What is it? Muadh said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Even a little showing-off is shirk. Whoever shows enmity to a friend of Allah has declared war against Allah. And indeed Allah loves those hidden God-fearing ones who, when absent from a gathering, are not missed, and when present, are not recognised; their hearts are lamps of guidance, found in dust-covered dark places. This hadith is sahih al-isnad but Imam Bukhari and Imam Muslim did not narrate it."
"7934","Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with them, narrates that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever sacrifices all desires for a single desire, Allah will suffice him in all his worldly and otherworldly affairs; and whoever lets his desires scatter, Allah does not care in which valley of the world he perishes. This hadith is sahih al-isnad but Imam Bukhari and Imam Muslim did not narrate it."
"7935","Abu Ubaydah bin al-Jarrah, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The heart of the son of Adam is like a sparrow, changing seven times in a day. This hadith is sahih according to the standard of Imam Muslim, but the two Shaykhs did not narrate it."
"7936","Abu Saeed al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Hidden shirk is that a man acts to please another human being. This hadith is sahih al-isnad but Imam Bukhari and Imam Muslim did not narrate it."
"7937","Yala bin Shaddad bin Aws narrates from his father that in the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, we used to regard showing-off as minor shirk. This hadith is sahih al-isnad but Imam Bukhari and Imam Muslim did not narrate it."
"7938","Abu Bakr Ismail bin Muhammad, the jurist of Rayy, narrated to us the hadith in full: Abu Hatim Muhammad bin Idris narrated to us, Affan bin Muslim narrated to us, Abdul Hamid bin Bahram narrated to us, Shahr bin Hawshab narrated to us, Abdur Rahman bin Ghanm narrated to us, from Shaddad bin Aws, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Whoever prays to show off has committed shirk, whoever fasts to show off has committed shirk, and whoever gives charity to show off has committed shirk. [Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi's summary] 7938 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."
"7939","Tawus narrates: A man said: O Prophet of Allah, I stand in many places seeking Allah's pleasure, yet alongside I also wish my station to become known. The narrator says: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, had not yet answered my question when this verse was revealed: So whoever hopes for the meeting with his Lord, let him do righteous deeds and associate none in the worship of his Lord. (Al-Kahf: 110)."
"7940","Abu Ahmad Bakr bin Muhammad bin Hamdan narrated to us, Abdus Samad bin al-Fadl narrated to us, Makki bin Ibrahim narrated to us, Abdul Wahid bin Zayd narrated to us, from Ubadah bin Nusayy, who said: I visited Shaddad bin Aws, may Allah be pleased with him, at his place of prayer while he was weeping. I said: O Abu Abdur Rahman, what makes you weep? He said: A hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. I said: What is it? He said: Once I was with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when I saw something on his face that displeased me. I said: May my father and mother be sacrificed for you, O Messenger of Allah, I see signs of worry on your blessed face; what is the matter? The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: A matter I fear for my Ummah after me. I asked: What is it? He said: Shirk and hidden lust. I said: O Messenger of Allah, will your Ummah fall into shirk after you? The Messenger of Allah said: O Shaddad, they will not worship the moon and the sun, nor worship any idol or stone; rather they will show off their deeds to people. I said: O Messenger of Allah, is showing-off shirk? He said: Yes. I asked: O Messenger of Allah, what is hidden lust? He said: People will fast in the morning, but then worldly lusts will overcome them, so they will break their fast."
"7941","Abu Dharr, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to me: Visit the graves, for it refreshes the remembrance of the Hereafter. And wash the dead, for washing a lifeless body and cleaning it is a mighty admonition. Attend funeral prayers; perhaps some grief will enter your heart, for the grief-stricken heart shall be under Allah's Throne on the Day of Judgment. This hadith is sahih al-isnad but Imam Bukhari and Imam Muslim did not narrate it."
"7942","Hani, the freed slave of Uthman bin Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates: I saw Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, standing by a grave weeping until his blessed beard became wet. He was asked: Paradise and Hell are mentioned in your presence, yet you do not weep so much at their mention, while standing by this grave you weep so much; why is that? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: The grave is the first station of the stations of the Hereafter; if one is saved from it, all stations after it are easier. And if one is not saved from it, those after it are even harsher. And the Messenger of Allah also said: I have never seen a sight more dreadful than the grave. This hadith is sahih al-isnad but Imam Bukhari and Imam Muslim did not narrate it."
"7943","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Jafar bin Yazid al-Qari al-Adami narrated to us in Baghdad, Abu Jafar Ahmad bin Ubayd bin Nasih al-Nahwi narrated to us, Muhammad bin Musab al-Qarqasai narrated to us, Abdur Rahman bin Amr al-Awzai narrated to me, Mak-hul narrated to me, from Ziyad bin Harithah, from Habib bin Maslamah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, invited retaliation against himself for a scratch he had unintentionally caused a Bedouin. Jibril, peace be upon him, came and said: O Muhammad, Allah did not send you as a tyrant or an arrogant one. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, called the Bedouin and said: Take retaliation from me. The Bedouin said: I have pardoned you, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you, O Messenger of Allah, and I could never do such a thing, however much you insist. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed for good for him. Ahmad Ubayd is alone in narrating this hadith from Muhammad bin Musab. Muhammad bin Musab is trustworthy."
"7944","It is narrated about Abu Dharr, may Allah be pleased with him, that he came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Ahl al-Bayt, I love you. The Prophet said to him: Do you say this swearing by Allah? He said: Yes, I swear by Allah. The Prophet said: Then prepare a shield against poverty, for poverty comes toward whoever loves us faster than a flood rushes from a mountain peak toward its depth. This hadith is sahih according to the standard of Imam Bukhari and Imam Muslim, but the two Shaykhs did not narrate it."
"7945","Miqdad bin Madikarib al-Kindi, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: A man never fills a worse vessel than his belly; three morsels suffice a man to keep his back straight. If he must eat more, then one third for food, one third for water, and one third for breathing. This hadith is sahih al-isnad but Imam Bukhari and Imam Muslim did not narrate it."
"7946","Muhammad bin Wasi al-Azdi narrates: I went to Bilal bin Abi Burdah bin Abi Musa and said: O Bilal, your father narrated to me from your grandfather this saying of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: In Hell there is a valley, and in the valley a well named Habhab. It is Allah's due right to cast every tyrant into it. So keep fearing Allah and do not become a dweller of that well. This hadith is sahih al-isnad but Imam Bukhari and Imam Muslim did not narrate it."
"7947","Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Love the poor and sit with them, love the Arabs from the depth of your heart, and keep away from people what you yourself consider harmful. If Umar al-Riyahi heard from Hajjaj bin Aswad, then this hadith is sahih al-isnad, but Imam Bukhari and Imam Muslim did not narrate it."
